# .book/.gitignore — BookBench default ignores for a book repository
# Generated by bookbench/templates/book/.gitignore (etap 08.1)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Voice profile (TOV-05): the author's voice is personal data and should not
# be committed to a public book repository by default. The voice itself lives
# in the personal library at ~/.bookbench/voices/ (TOV-02), portable across
# books via /bookbench:voice extract|save-as|import|list.
#
# If you are running a public research project and DO want to commit the
# voice (e.g. to share writing style as part of an experiment), comment out
# the two lines below or override with `!path/to/file` later in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
context/voice-profile.md
agent-guidelines/writer/voice-samples.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Marketer voice (TOV-10): independent from book voice; same privacy logic.
# Filled by book-marketer first-run interview, lives only in the book repo.
# Comment out if you want to share marketing voice publicly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
agent-guidelines/marketer/brand-voice.md
agent-guidelines/marketer/telegram-tone.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other entries can be added by the author manually below this line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
